title: Crystal Voids
manual: structure/#c2-packing

Measures the empty space in a crystal: the volume of the unit cell not occupied by the
atoms. Three definitions of "empty space" are available, one per tab, and each
reports the void volume and its fraction of the cell volume. The analysis needs a periodic
cell, so it is only available for crystals.

# Isosurface tab

In this tab, the empty space is the volume where the promolecular
density (the sum of free-atom densities) is lower than a certain
value.

- "Isovalue (a.u.)": a point belongs to a void if the promolecular
  density at that point is lower than this value.
- "Grid spacing (Å)": approximate distance between consecutive points of the grid on which
  the promolecular density is calculated. A finer grid resolves the voids better but takes
  longer (the grid size is shown next to it).
- "Calculate": calculates the density on the grid and groups the points below the isovalue
  into voids.
- "Visualize isosurface": draws the isosurface that bounds the voids in the view. "Create
  Object" copies it into a permanent object, editable from the Objects menu of the view.

# Polyhedra tab

In the polyhedra tab, empty space is whatever is left after
coordination polyhedra are drawn.

- "Center" and "Vertices": species of the atoms at the center and at the vertices of the
  coordination polyhedra (several species can be ticked).
- "Distance range (Å)": shortest and longest center-vertex distance that makes an atom a
  vertex. "Reset" restores the defaults for this system.
- "Visualize polyhedra": draws the polyhedra in the view.

# Packing tab

In the packing tab, spheres are placed on atoms and empty space
corresponds to those points outside an atomic sphere.

- "Atomic radii": van der Waals, covalent, or half the nearest-neighbor distance, as in the
  PACKING keyword.
- "Scale": factor multiplying the radius of every atom.
- "Precision": the sphere volume is found by Monte Carlo sampling, which stops when its
  standard deviation divided by the volume reaches this value.
- "Calculate" and "Visualize spheres", as in the other tabs.

# Results

Each tab has a Results section with the volumes, the cell volume and the percentages. The
Isosurface tab also lists every void (volume, density minimum, density there), the Polyhedra
tab each polyhedron (atom, multiplicity, vertices, distances, volume), and the Packing tab
gives the packing ratio.
